  "articleBody": "Upgrading small hardware or swapping an existing mirror is a straightforward weekend job. However, once a bathroom upgrade touches underlying systems, bringing in a professional general contractor protects your home from serious structural and water issues.\n\nWhen Professional Guidance Helps\n\n- Hidden Water Intrusion: Soft spots in the subfloor around the toilet, musty smells behind baseboards, or stained drywall indicate active moisture that requires structural evaluation and framing repairs.\n- Moving Major Plumbing Lines: Shifting a drain, venting stack, or water supply requires opening walls and evaluating joist layouts. Keeping plumbing in its existing position simplifies construction, but relocating fixtures requires licensed trade coordination.\n- Electrical Circuit Updates: Adding modern lighting, heat fans, or multiple outlets requires dedicated GFCI protection under building codes to prevent shock hazards and overloaded breakers.\n- Advanced Shower Waterproofing: Tile work only lasts as long as the waterproofing membrane behind it. Professional installation ensures shower pans and wall assemblies stay watertight.\n- Permit-Required Structural Changes: Widening an entrance for accessibility, moving walls, or modifying load-bearing studs needs proper oversight to remain code-compliant.\n\nWhen you want an experienced craftsman to manage your bathroom remodel, reach out to Abraham Becerra at HH Remodeling LLC at 303-505-0866 for dependable, quality work across the Denver area.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
